* JUMP - EXECUTE AT A MEMORY ADDRESS

SYSOP ONLY. Private utility; use the local sysop console.

A - Purpose, syntax and examples

:A
* JUMP - EXECUTE AT A MEMORY ADDRESS

SYSOP ONLY. Private utility; use the local sysop console.

Syntax:
    JUMP hex-address [command-tail]

Transfers execution to a specified hexadecimal address and supplies the
optional command tail.

An incorrect address can execute data or damage the running environment.
Reserved for private program development; it is not an ordinary way to
start a COM file.

See HELP COMMANDS for the command index.
